        "apiVersion": "hololab.dev/v1",
        "category": "reconstruction/megasam",
        "description": "Standardize MegaSAM camera trajectories and depth-backprojected per-frame points as three timed colmap4d components.",
        "docs": "Repository-owned MegaSAM chain: Depth-Anything, UniDepth, camera tracking, RAFT and CVD. Outputs camera trajectories and depth-backprojected per-frame points, plus independent images. No SHARP or Gaussian inference. Binary colmap4d components require assembly before validate_full. No exposure metadata input in 0.6.1: video defaults to pts_estimate; uniform video timing requires fps_num/fps_den; image arrays require frames_fps. Times are explicitly estimated, not measured exposure truth. All source scripts/checkpoints resolve within this repository; subprocesses use the node-selected logical runtime interpreter. See packs/megasam-track@0.6.1/README.md.",
        "exec": {
          "shell": "set -euo pipefail\npython \"{{ package_root }}/packs/megasam-track@0.6.1/run.py\" <<'PACK_CONFIG'\n{{ {'params': params, 'inputs': inputs, 'outputs': outputs, 'scratch': scratch_dir} | tojson }}\nPACK_CONFIG\n"
        },
